{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1522640-low-essence-alchemical-colossi-and-metropoli","id":1522640,"title":"Low-Essence Alchemical Colossi and Metropoli?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Alchemical Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-15T12:36:51-07:00","id":1522640,"title":"Low-Essence Alchemical Colossi and Metropoli?","content":"I had an interesting thought today. With 3e's reduction in focus on high-Essence play, I'm wondering if we might see a shift in the design of Alchemicals to put Colossi and even Metropoli into the &quot;playable&quot; Essence ranges. Given where Warstrider Evocations start, it might be the case that Alchemicals as young as Essence 2 might be eligible for refit into Colossi. Given how the Essence 10 characters of 2nd edition are now Essence 7 at most, Metropoli starting at Essence 5 could be in the cards. If such were the case, what would you want to see?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-15T23:29:22-07:00","id":1522659,"title":"","content":"Colossi probably will be playable just fine. There are rules for Legendary Size for other Exalts as-is, though Alchemicals likely have to take into account some penalites for being that permanently. Rather than a natural outgrowth of Essence it probalby is something a character installs in and out of.<br /> <br /> On becoming a polis, my guess is that will be left for higher Essence stuff. It's something that never was supported before and to be frank, I don't see what is gained by tyring to support it in actual play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-16T04:24:01-07:00","id":1522666,"title":"","content":"I've previously suggested that Architects would be a decent framework for portraying the drone-body avatar of an Alchemical City.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T12:56:02-07:00","id":1522720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1522640-low-essence-alchemical-colossi-and-metropoli?p=1522659#post1522659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather than a natural outgrowth of Essence it probalby is something a character installs in and out of.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt being a Colossus will be something temporary. Otherwise, it's just an Alchemical piloting a Warstrider.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's something that never was supported before and to be frank, I don't see what is gained by tyring to support it in actual play. </div> </div> </div>Think of it as the ultimate way of developing a location. There's no way a player would ever be more invested in a place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T12:56:51-07:00","id":1523652,"title":"","content":"I think if it isn't supported I'd probably look at either making or finding homebrew charms that would let you &quot;transform&quot; into a robot mode along with a charm that allows one of your drones to summon your colossus form to its location, same with your patropoli form","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T09:57:25-07:00","id":1524816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1522640-low-essence-alchemical-colossi-and-metropoli?p=1522720#post1522720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think of it as the ultimate way of developing a location.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find that the things that make the cities found in Compass: Authochthonia most interesting and memorable can be translated in principle to just about any place where lots of people live and significant and dramatic events happen. There's nothing about the Glass Market that makes it fundamentally impossible to take place anywhere besides inside an Alchemical Exalt.<br /> <br /> And indeed, the Metropolis has very little, if any, personal engagement with that practice, compared to what even a Dragon-Blood would do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no way a player would ever be more invested in a place.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if they conducted an annual festival in which one could be an actual participant, especially if it was one they founded in order to bind some community more closely together or promote some value.<br /> <br /> &quot;Playing Augustus reshaping the institutions of the Republic into all being under his sway without friction or uprising and creating a public persona as unto a living god is all well and good, but just imagine what it would be like to play the platform from which he makes the speeches, or periodically rolling dice to ensure the aqueduct water is clean and fresh.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not to mention the capacity to go away from the place and do things on its behalf.<br /> <br /> I don't doubt that there have been some throwaway lines about cities being able to have drone bodies, but not only do they have so sense of presence in the setting, I find the whole idea of them to be incompatible with the idea of the cities in the first place, being, as they are, places first and foremost. You either retain the point where human personality becomes diffuse in a way that keeps it from getting in the way of being settings for municipal stories, in which case such drones don't really have anything to express, or else cities get rewritten to be more relatable in a way that runs interference with the usual kinds of social and political drama. And at the point where they're being given remote bodies that can do everything from before the transformation, why even bother having them transform at all? Might as well just have it that cities pop out of the metal and are subject to the whims of the one powerful Alchemical (never mind what that does to the dynamic between them and society).<br /> <br /> Yeesh, even if one took the idea that the biggest way for a player to care about something is to actually be the thing (&quot;after all, how can I possibly care for something else more than myself&quot;), &quot;investment&quot; seems like a pretty thin addition to the pro list compared to being functionally playable.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T10:54:56-08:00","id":1525081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1522640-low-essence-alchemical-colossi-and-metropoli?p=1524816#post1524816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find that the things that make the cities found in Compass: Authochthonia most interesting and memorable can be translated in principle to just about any place where lots of people live and significant and dramatic events happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is sad, because a city that is itself a person should have shown definite impacts from that difference, in many of the same ways that Mother Bog differs from an ordinary swamp. I blame the Elder Exalt problem that 2nd Edition had. The setting had to work very hard to keep all the Essence 10 characters that could squash a circle of protagonists or solve all the interesting problems of the world doing nothing despite having such massive personal power. Autochthonia had an advantage by making all the highest Essence characters largely sessile, but if Alchemical cities had been handled as characters as well as places, there would have been difficulties making things such as major criminal organizations seem plausible. How would you get away planning a criminal conspiracy to siphon nutrient slurry when the walls have literal eyes and ears?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What if they conducted an annual festival in which one could be an actual participant, especially if it was one they founded in order to bind some community more closely together or promote some value. </div> </div> </div>You are describing something that an Alchemical city could do while also being the venue for the event.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't doubt that there have been some throwaway lines about cities being able to have drone bodies, </div> </div> </div>Avatar-Launching Silo was one of the first Municipal Charms mentioned by name. It was incorporated into the setting lore, particularly with Ixut's ghost. It very much wasn't a throwaway line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You either retain the point where human personality becomes diffuse in a way that keeps it from getting in the way of being settings for municipal stories, in which case such drones don't really have anything to express, or else cities get rewritten to be more relatable in a way that runs interference with the usual kinds of social and political drama. </div> </div> </div>I think you are lacking in vision and imagination here. Have you ever read The City Who Fought by Anne McCaffery? It's set in the same universe as The Ship Who Sang. The city in question is a person, a human who has lived all their life wired into technology, who administrates the autonomous and semi-autonomous systems on a space station. The city has a broad range of abilities, from surveillance to door locks, but is also limited by what systems are automated and by being only able to focus on a limited number of things at any given time. Making the person of an Alchemical city into an important part of how that city operates without also obviating normal social and political drama is more than possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeesh, even if one took the idea that the biggest way for a player to care about something is to actually be the thing (&quot;after all, how can I possibly care for something else more than myself&quot;), </div> </div> </div>More like &quot;I care about this place so much that I have made it the way in which I interact with the world, such that all my attempts to alter the wider setting must originate here&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;investment&quot; seems like a pretty thin addition to the pro list compared to being functionally playable. </div> </div> </div>We already have Charms that explore space that would make Alchemical cities playable, such as the Lunar territory Charms. Being playable takes effort that I doubt we would see to the level of a full splat book, but we might see something along the lines of the abbreviated Charm sets from Exigents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T21:03:13-08:00","id":1525106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1522640-low-essence-alchemical-colossi-and-metropoli?p=1525081#post1525081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We already have Charms that explore space that would make Alchemical cities playable, such as the Lunar territory Charms. Being playable takes effort that I doubt we would see to the level of a full splat book, but we might see something along the lines of the abbreviated Charm sets from Exigents.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is the first time I've seen someone advocate using Lunar mechanics for Alchemical Charms instead of, you know, the reverse. (^VVVVVVVV^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T11:39:28-08:00","id":1525466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1522640-low-essence-alchemical-colossi-and-metropoli?p=1525081#post1525081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The setting had to work very hard to keep all the Essence 10 characters that could squash a circle of protagonists or solve all the interesting problems of the world doing nothing despite having such massive personal power.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only Essence 10 characters I can recall besides Chejop Kejak (closed Charm set and the stricter limits to range of even Sidereal Martial Arts) were some of the Deathlords, who weren't exactly invested in <i>solving</i> problems.<br /> <br /> Second Edition would have had a much easier time of things if it had proceeded from how characters like Ma-Ha-Suchi were portrayed first, rather than giving them ridiculous powers and then twisting back upon themselves to explain how and why the firmly established setting position of elder Exalted could still function.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you get away planning a criminal conspiracy to siphon nutrient slurry when the walls have literal eyes and ears?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... yeah, the game does need to prioritise the existence of challenges that can be engaged with at the level where the majority of play actually happens.<br /> <br /> I think the fiction still provides something for the Alchemical cities to be and do by virtue of the extreme unsuitability of their world for human life and habitation. People sacrificing the capability for governing how the people within the city will conduct their lives in exchange for being the foundational infrastructure of a water purification system. The proposition that they can do both does have to resolve the question of what that allows the majority of Alchemicals to still do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are describing something that an Alchemical city could do while also being the venue for the event.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does being the venue contribute that makes it a profoundly greater sense of investment than all of the stuff that is conducted on the scale of human interaction and engagement?<br /> <br /> And indeed, if the Alchemical loses the human scale, then it's not <i>all</i> stuff that can be retained. If they don't lose human scale, it ends up back in the area of accumulating enough positions for themselves that it edges out the commonly played Alchemicals (and maybe lessons the significance and grandeur of transforming into cities).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was incorporated into the setting lore, particularly with Ixut's ghost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you elaborate?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you are lacking in vision and imagination here. Have you ever read The City Who Fought by Anne McCaffery? It's set in the same universe as The Ship Who Sang. The city in question is a person, a human who has lived all their life wired into technology, who administrates the autonomous and semi-autonomous systems on a space station. The city has a broad range of abilities, from surveillance to door locks, but is also limited by what systems are automated and by being only able to focus on a limited number of things at any given time. Making the person of an Alchemical city into an important part of how that city operates without also obviating normal social and political drama is more than possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like interesting prose but fairly limited for being actively controlled by a player character.<br /> <br /> Referencing the limitations of automated systems appears to be acknowledgement that maintaining consistency in the idea of Alchemical cities necessitates immobilising them, but doesn't really address how such immobility can make for engaging gameplay.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We already have Charms that explore space that would make Alchemical cities playable, such as the Lunar territory Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how. The Charisma Charms are mostly ways to project influence or provide minor bonuses through a defined area (with one Charm to let them divert injuries), the Wits Charms are primarily creating and manipulating some hidden spaces and a few ways to leverage penalties and environmental hazards against intruders (and a few things to ward from the Wyld). I hardly see anything that could be translated into the experience of playing the territory itself rather than a person harnessing it as a resource, and more than a couple that I find heavily predicated on the capacity for the Lunar to be a mobile actor within and without it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T12:02:23-08:00","id":1525467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1522640-low-essence-alchemical-colossi-and-metropoli?p=1525466#post1525466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Can you elaborate?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ghost Ixut can maim his po to produce a Shadow, a Colossus-body explicitly created through the remains of the city's Avatar-Launching Silo, which is mentioned by name alongside some other Municipal Charms. Shadows can also kind of operate some of the ruins of the blasted Municipal Charms to send pulses of lightning through it or see through its former surveillance system, for the noted example effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-19T19:16:51-08:00","id":1527104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1522640-low-essence-alchemical-colossi-and-metropoli?p=1525466#post1525466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only Essence 10 characters I can recall besides Chejop Kejak (closed Charm set and the stricter limits to range of even Sidereal Martial Arts) were some of the Deathlords, who weren't exactly invested in <i>solving</i> problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are taking me a little literally there, given I mentioned the Elder Exalt problem. It's not just the Deathlords and Chejop Kejak. It's the Unconquered Sun, Luna, the Maidens, Gaia, the Great Elemental Dragons, the elder Sidereals, the elder Lunars, and even the elder Terrestrials. Second Edition had a whole lot of powerful people sitting in holding patterns that could have been almost unopposable if they just got up and did something. The Mask of Winters conquering Thorns showed just how dangerous he was, but now be just keeps Juggernaut parked outside instead of conquering the neighbors. Etc. Etc. This problem has been hashed to death before and thankfully has been mostly resolved in Third Edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the fiction still provides something for the Alchemical cities to be and do by virtue of the extreme unsuitability of their world for human life and habitation. People sacrificing the capability for governing how the people within the city will conduct their lives in exchange for being the foundational infrastructure of a water purification system. </div> </div> </div>If I'm following you correctly, you think that Alchemical cities should no longer be agents in any meaningful sense. I think such a stance discards the aspects that make genius loci such as Alchemical cities interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The proposition that they can do both does have to resolve the question of what that allows the majority of Alchemicals to still do. </div> </div> </div>And that is resolved in much the same way that the Lunar and Sidereal elder problem was. Alchemical cities can't be everywhere at once and their powers aren't beyond those of Champions in terms of intensity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200b<br /> What does being the venue contribute that makes it a profoundly greater sense of investment than all of the stuff that is conducted on the scale of human interaction and engagement? </div> </div> </div>Because it is all of the stuff conducted on the scale of human interaction and engagement and then more. You cared enough about these people that you became their home in the most literal sense possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200b<br /> And indeed, if the Alchemical loses the human scale, then it's not <i>all</i> stuff that can be retained. If they don't lose human scale, it ends up back in the area of accumulating enough positions for themselves that it edges out the commonly played Alchemicals (and maybe lessons the significance and grandeur of transforming into cities). </div> </div> </div>You are engaging in a lot of black and white thinking here. There is a broad spectrum between &quot;Unable to operate at human scale&quot; and &quot;renders all other Alchemicals obsolete&quot;. A city can be capable of a lot without being able to do everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200b<br /> That sounds like interesting prose but fairly limited for being actively controlled by a player character.<br /> <br /> Referencing the limitations of automated systems appears to be acknowledgement that maintaining consistency in the idea of Alchemical cities necessitates immobilising them, but doesn't really address how such immobility can make for engaging gameplay. </div> </div> </div>In many of the same ways that a game set entirely in Nexus can make for engaging gameplay. Instead of globe trotting, you deal with the problems of this place. You resolve factional disputes, resource shortages, defend against local threats. You just do it with a modified set of tools.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200b<br /> I don't see how. The Charisma Charms are mostly ways to project influence or provide minor bonuses through a defined area (with one Charm to let them divert injuries), the Wits Charms are primarily creating and manipulating some hidden spaces and a few ways to leverage penalties and environmental hazards against intruders (and a few things to ward from the Wyld). I hardly see anything that could be translated into the experience of playing the territory itself rather than a person harnessing it as a resource, and more than a couple that I find heavily predicated on the capacity for the Lunar to be a mobile actor within and without it. </div> </div> </div>You are looking at a few footsteps into a large space and not seeing ways that they could be expanded. No other canon Exalt type has as deep a connection to a place as an Alchemical city except maybe an Architect (though Architects are stuck at Terrestrial levels of power). Mechanisms for awareness across large spaces, environmental control, automated defenses, terraforming, and more are untapped design space because it isn't appropriate to other Exalts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}